  <!--
    The two Closeness overrides in this file, and the only two. Closeness is normally MEASURED -
    beds against the ground the tier stands on - and the measurement is right for every other
    design here. It is wrong for exactly one shape: a design that raises SEVERAL DWELLINGS AT
    ONCE inside one plot. Three households around a square, or a whole terraced street, put a lot
    of beds on a little ground and read as one packed room, when what is actually there is the
    stone house's own walls repeated. So both declare the stone house's rung. Note that the XL
    housing court needs no override: at seven cells a bed it already measures Roomed.
  -->
