  <!-- ======================================================================== WATER ==
    There are no wells. New water comes from patient collection, from the salt-pan, from
    trade, or from great machinery hauled home and certified - never from a hole in the
    ground, because in Qud water is money and nothing mints money quietly.

    Two lanes open at camp and they are honestly different. The catchment wants weather and
    no crew; the salt-pan wants a crew and no weather, which is why it is the answer on dry
    ground and the only water work that goes underground. Everything above them stores
    rather than makes: a cistern raises the sustainable level because it carries the
    settlement across the dry stretch, not because it conjures a dram.
  -->
  <building Key="saltpan" DisplayName="salt-pan (slow, salty work; a little fresh water and the salt it was hiding)" Blueprint="r_KingdomSaltPan"
            Cost="4" Ticks="1800" Styles="all" Category="storage" Plot="S" Open="yes"
            Materials="stone:4" Staff="1" Manning="scaled" Carries="water:2"
            UpgradesTo="saltterrace" />
