  <!-- ====================================================================== DEFENSE ==
    A wall is not a plot. Anything carrying a Defence rating is sited on the frontier of the
    claim, one cell at a time, which is why no entry here that defends declares a Plot at all -
    a design that claimed both a defence rating and a plot would be sited on the wall and its
    plot would never be laid.

    The gatehouse is a placement rule rather than a size: it belongs where the wall meets a
    road. Until roads exist to meet - they are meant to be worn into the ground by real settler
    routes, not drawn - it is sited as an ordinary length of wall and named honestly as the one
    place the wall gives way. The barracks is the exception that proves the rule - it houses
    the watch, so it stands on real ground inside the wall and offers no Defence of its own.
    What defends is the people it holds.
  -->
  <building Key="palisade" DisplayName="thorn palisade" Blueprint="r_KingdomPalisade"
            Cost="6" Ticks="1800" Styles="all" Category="defense"
